  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN227-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉkaṇ vēṟupaṭṭa talaimakaṭkut tōḻi colliyatūumām. talaimakaḷatu vēṟupā<space quantity="9" unit="character"></space> tōḻikkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">It is also what the confidante said to HER who had undergone changes during the separation from [HIM]. (What was said to the confidante who <space quantity="9" unit="character"></space> the changes in HER.)</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN227.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>nutalpacan taṉṟē tōḷcā yiṉavē</l>
        <l>titalai yalkul variyum vāṭiṉa</l>
        <l>veṉṉā kuvaḷko livaḷeṉap paṉmā</l>
        <l>ṇīrmali kaṇṇoṭu neṭituniṉain tēṟṟi</l>
        <l>yiṉaiyal vāḻi tōḻi naṉaikavu<supplied>ṭ</supplied></l>
        <l>kāy<supplied>ci</supplied>ṉañ ciṟanta vāypuku <anchor n="2"/>kaṭāttoṭu</l>
        <l>muṉṉilai peṟāatu muraṇip poṉṉiṇarp</l>
        <l>pulikkēḻ vēṅkaip pūñciṉai pulampa</l>
        <l>mutalpāyn tiṭṭa muḻuvali yorutta<supplied>l</supplied></l>
        <l>cennilap <anchor n="3"/>paṭunī ṟāṭic cerumalaintu</l>
        <l>kaḷaṅko<supplied>ḷ</supplied> maḷḷariṉ muḻaṅku mattam</l>
        <l>palaviṟan takaṉṟaṉa rāyiṉu nilaii</l>
        <l>nōyila rākanaṅ kātalar vāyvāṭ</l>
        <l>ṭamiḻakap paṭutta vimiḻicai muraciṉ</l>
        <l>varunar varaiyāp perunā ḷirukkait</l>
        <l>tūṅkal pāṭiya vōṅkuperu nallicaip</l>
        <l>piṭimiti vaḻutuṇaip perumpeyart taḻumpaṉ</l>
        <l>kaṭimatil varaippi ṉūṇū rumpar<anchor n="4"/></l>
        <l>viḻuniti tuñcum vīṟupeṟu tirunaka</l>
        <l>riruṅkaḻip paṭappai maruṅkūrp paṭṭiṉat</l>
        <l>tellimi ḻāva<supplied>ṇat</supplied> taṉṉa</l>
        <l>kalleṉ kampalai ceytakaṉ ṟōrē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">“The forehead has turned pale. The shoulders are emaciated.</l>
        <l corresp="2">The lines on the hips with beauty spots have faded.</l>
        <l corresp="3a-c">What will become of her?” so thinking</l>
        <l corresp="3d-4">[and] reflecting long, many times, with eyes full of tears,</l>
        <l corresp="5a-c 12c">don’t despair, oh friend. Even though</l>
        <l corresp="11d-12c">he departed, traversing roads many,</l>
        <l>where the male in [its] full strength that had, with ichor entering</l>
        <l>[its] mouth from [its] wet temples when excelling in hot anger,</l>
        <l>been opposed [to the tiger] without obtaining a [direct confrontation]</l>
        <l>leapt against the [tree] trunk so that the flowering branches of the kino tree,</l>
        <l>with tiger lustre in golden clusters, are lonely,</l>
        <l>bathed in the dust rising from the red ground, [and], facing the fight,</l>
        <l corresp="5d-11c">thunders like warriors taking the battlefield,</l>
        <l corresp="12d-13c">let our lover permanently be without pain,</l>
        <l corresp="22">– him who departed making a racket, noisily,</l>
        <l corresp="21">like the bazaar  buzzling with light</l>
        <l corresp="20">of the maritime Maruṅkūr with a garden by the dark backwaters,</l>
        <l corresp="19">a brilliant town  that has obtained distinction, where great treasure sleeps,</l>
        <l corresp="18">beyond Ūṇūr in the region of protected fortifications</l>
        <l corresp="17">[belonging to] Taḻumpaṉ of great name for the brinjal trampled by the she-elephant(?)</l>
        <l corresp="16">of high great fame that is sung while swaying</l>
        <l corresp="15">on [his] seat on a great day when there is no limit to those who come,</l>
        <l corresp="14">with a drum of buzzing sound that is beaten in the land of Tamil,</l>
        <l corresp="13d">with an excellent sword. (13d)</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
